{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 34, :comments ["<b>And the field of the open land of their cities shall not be sold.</b> Sale by the treasurer — for if a Levite consecrated his field and did not redeem it and the treasurer sold it, it does not go to the priests at the Jubilee as is said regarding Israel: ״וְאִם מָכַר אֶת הַשָּׂדֶה לְאִישׁ אַחֵר לֹא יִגָּאֵל עוֹד״ (Leviticus 27) — but a Levite redeems forever."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:08:23.376233584Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}